
use two seperate terminals, both from the repo root
(setup: python3.12 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt)

*run actual arm (Linux port is usually /dev/ttyACM0, Mac is /dev/tty.usbmodem...; find it with: lerobot-find-port)
python reverse_kinematics/testing_folow_point.py --urdf hardware_test/SO-ARM100/Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.urdf --port /dev/ttyACM0 --execute --relative --reach 0.08

*try without hardware first (gripper traces a small circle)
python reverse_kinematics/testing_folow_point.py --urdf hardware_test/SO-ARM100/Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.urdf --demo

*send information to socket
python -c "
import socket, time
s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)
for _ in range(90):
    s.sendto(b'0 0 0.02', ('127.0.0.1', 5005))
    time.sleep(1/30)
"
